{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2022-03-02 06:45:00', 'title': 'PFIZER GRANTED FDA BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION FOR RESPIRATORY SYNCYTIAL VIRUS (RSV) VACCINE CANDIDATE FOR THE PREVENTION OF RSV IN INFANTS FROM BIRTH UP TO SIX MONTHS OF AGE BY ACTIVE IMMUNIZATION OF PREGNANT WOMEN', 'text': 'NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PFIZER INC. (NYSE:PFE) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT ITS RESPIRATORY SYNCYTIAL VIRUS (RSV) VACCINE CANDIDATE, PF-06482077 OR RSVPREF, RECEIVED BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION FROM THE US FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) FOR PREVENTION OF RSV-ASSOCIATED LOWER RESPIRATORY TRACT ILLNESS IN INFANTS FROM BIRTH UP TO SIX MONTHS OF AGE BY ACTIVE IMMUNIZATION OF PREGNANT WOMEN. THE FDA DECISION IS INFORMED BY THE RESULTS OF THE PHASE 2B PROOF-OF-CONCEPT STUDY OF RSVPREF (NCT0403209'}